-- title:
--   Rank of [p^v]_F is p^{vh} for a formal group of height h
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $p$ a prime, $d$ a natural number, and let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: a $d$-tuple $F_1,\dots,F_d$ of power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with zero constant term, whose linear parts satisfy $\mathrm{coeff}_{X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}}F_i = \mathrm{coeff}_{X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}}F_i = \delta_{ij}$, and which is associative in the usual sense $F(F(X,Y),Z) = F(X,F(Y,Z))$ as an identity of substitutions; assume moreover that $F$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each $F_i$. For $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $F.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,n : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ denote the multiplication-by-$n$ series, defined recursively by $[0]_F = 0$ and $[n+1]_F{}_i = F_i([n]_F(X), X)$. Suppose that for some $h \in \mathbb{N}$ the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $[p]_F$ has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Then for every $v \in \mathbb{N}$ the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of $[p^v]_F$ has $k$-dimension $p^{v h}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the order of the $p^v$-torsion of a commutative formal group of height $h$ over a field is $p^{vh}$: the ranks multiply along the iterated substitution $X \mapsto [p]_F(X)$, whose finiteness and flatness come from [`MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient). It is used in the treatment of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules and their isogenies in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd material, where heights of $p$-power multiplication maps must be computed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_pow_eq_pow.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_BasicV2

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open MvPowerSeries

universe u

theorem MvFormalGroup.finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_pow_eq_pow
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {d : ℕ} (F : MvFormalGroup d k) [F.IsComm] (h : ℕ)
    (hh : Module.finrank k (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range (F.nthSeries p))) = p ^ h)
    (v : ℕ) :
    Module.finrank k (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range (F.nthSeries (p ^ v)))) =
      p ^ (v * h) := by sorry
